  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with PCA (config_001, acc=0.485) dominates both image-only baselines (acc≈0.21-0.23), establishing RNA as the primary signal. The RNA encoder choice is the most fundamental untested design variable. Question: Does a learned nonlinear encoder (scvi_n200) capture structure that linear PCA misses, improving on the 0.485 baseline? This is a clean single-variable comparison to config_001 (only the encoder changes, keeping singleprofile and no aggregation). Why this is the best next step: With 6 experiments remaining, identifying the superior RNA encoder before exploring multiprofile or multimodal fusion ensures we build subsequent experiments on the strongest foundation. If scvi_n200 outperforms PCA, it opens a promising branch (configs 005-006, 028-039); if not, we confirm PCA suffices and can redirect budget toward profile aggregation or fusion. Testing image-based multimodal fusion is deprioritized given the large performance gap."
}

